# MC-X-F6, undecided. L §4.4: "Equal intervals from different reads stay undecided", and so do overlapping ones; L
# §5.12 Sort: "An order that can't be decided (a hole) is refused (RUN-ORDER)"; L §8.4 RUN-ORDER `fill <f>: the order
# of <arc> is a hole`. Two lots dated by overlapping windows (2027-02-01 .. 2027-02-28, 2027-02-10 .. 2027-03-15):
# the fill's sort can't order them, and every take is refused (the arc named is the one the sort met).
# tally 2.2.1 (#213, S-213; L §5.12 step 2: "but where only a window leaves it open it is HOLE-IMPRECISE (§4.4)"): the
# order is the windows' hole, not RUN-ORDER: on the days they differ the takes are 1, 0, 0, 1, on a day both lots share
# the tie changes a take (RUN-TIE), a refusal only some days give; every take is the hole naming both days.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): restated so the window sits in an attribute, not the movement's day: a window that
# reaches a move's `on` is a hole day (L §4.4), so the order the test is about reads the attribute.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source src "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind lots: event certain
  attr bought: date
index ids = [x1, x2]
input day[i in ids]: date
input d0: date
move lot[i in ids]: lots
  on d0
  attr bought = day[i]
fill f
  supply 1 for l in lots over ..
  demand 1 for c in lots over ..
  arc true
  order l.bought, c.bought
version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2027-01-01
  d0 = 2027-01-05
  day[x1] = window(2027-02-01, 2027-02-28)
  day[x2] = window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15)
ask t: f.taken[l, c] for l in lots over .., c in lots over ..
=== expect
t (l = lot[x1], c = lot[x1]): ?"date within window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15) not precise enough for the order of fill f" (day[x2])
  unknown day: day[x1]
  unknown day: day[x2]
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x1], c = lot[x2]): ?"date within window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15) not precise enough for the order of fill f" (day[x2])
  unknown day: day[x1]
  unknown day: day[x2]
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x2], c = lot[x1]): ?"date within window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15) not precise enough for the order of fill f" (day[x2])
  unknown day: day[x1]
  unknown day: day[x2]
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x2], c = lot[x2]): ?"date within window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15) not precise enough for the order of fill f" (day[x2])
  unknown day: day[x1]
  unknown day: day[x2]
  cut 2027-01-01
